#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"Reference documentation for the system-files interface, which grants snaps "
"access to specified system files and directories, including privileged data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:8
msgid "system-files interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `system-files` interface enables a snap to access specific system files "
"and directories (such as files in `/etc`). Consequently,  the interface can "
"provide access to privileged system data and is not connected by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"This interface is typically used to provide read-only access to system "
"configuration directories created by a non-snap version of an application "
"now running from an equivalent snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:14
msgid "<h2 id='heading--example'>Example</h2>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"The [Firefox](https://snapcraft.io/firefox), [Chromium](https://snapcraft.io/"
"chromium) and [Thunderbird](https://snapcraft.io/thunderbird) snaps use this "
"interface to enable access to system-installed policies to customise each "
"respective application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:18
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Interface management <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-connect-"
"interfaces>` and {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` for "
"further details on how interfaces are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:21
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:23
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:23
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:38
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:26
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"`read` (plug): list of files and/or directories for read-only access (eg, "
"'`read: [ /etc/file-read, /etc/dir-read ]`'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"`write` (plug): list of files and/or directories for read/write access (eg, "
"'`write: [ /etc/file-write, /etc/dir-write ]`'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:30
msgid "Requires snapd version _2.37+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"Consumers of this interface require a {ref}`snap declaration <interfaces-"
"process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>` for distribution via the "
"[Snap Store](https://snapcraft.io/store) and acceptance in the store "
"requires that the interface is not be used to access:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:33
msgid ""
"system files where the snap is not the clear owner (eg, /dev, /proc, /sys, /"
"usr, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"paths in `/dev`, such as `/dev/sda1` Access to `/dev` device nodes requires "
"both AppArmor policy and device control group inclusion, but the _system-"
"files_ interface does not have enough information to generate the necessary "
"policy to enable these use cases. As such, purpose-specific interfaces "
"should be used instead, such as  {ref}`block-devices <interfaces-block-"
"devices-interface>` or {ref}`raw-volume <interfaces-raw-volume-interface>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:38
msgid ""
"ⓘ  Do not share data between snaps. </br>While `system-files` can be used to "
"share data with another snap, such as within a configuration file, this "
"behaviour is not recommended. The {ref}`content interface <interfaces-"
"content-interface>` should be used instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"An additional requirement for acceptance in the Global store is using a "
"descriptive interface reference for use with `snap connections|interfaces|"
"connect|disconnect`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:45
msgid ""
"For example, the 'foo' application is packaged as a snap and the snap "
"publisher wants to import existing configuration from `/etc/foo` into the "
"snap. The snapcraft.yaml might be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:47
msgid ""
"name: foo\n"
"...\n"
"plugs:\n"
"  etc-foo:\n"
"    interface: system-files\n"
"    read:\n"
"    - /etc/foo\n"
"\n"
"apps:\n"
"  foo:\n"
"    plugs:\n"
"    - etc-foo\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:63
msgid ""
"Note, when declaring an instance of the `system-files` plug as above, it "
"should be named with a descriptive name that indicates to a user what access "
"it grants. In this case, the name `etc-foo` is used to reflect the access to "
"`/etc/foo`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/system-files-interface.md:65
msgid ""
"With the above, a `snap connect` command would look like: `snap connect "
"foo:etc-foo`."
msgstr ""

